fDay61Sec, lastMinOfDay59Sec, notInSync}</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">notInSync = Not in sync, indicates receiver did not get leap second info yet, conversion to UTC is not possible</td></tr><tr><td>Clock Stratum (clockStratum)</td><td></td><td>clockStratum=&lt;int&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>The number of hops required for the antenna to reach a valid reference clock. Acceptable range is 1-16 with 1 denoting a direct connection to a timing source and 16 denoting that the antenna is synchronized with a valid</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5557731986045837, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(498.9575500488281), np.float64(445.0718994140625)), (np.float64(498.9575500488281), np.float64(3117.772705078125)), (np.float64(2643.344970703125), np.float64(3117.772705078125)), (np.float64(2643.344970703125), np.float64(445.0718994140625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T20:02:08', 'text_as_html': '<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Miscellaneous and Custom Commands. ‘y’ command may to be used to send custom asynchronous messages to the antenna in a key- value pair formatted string. Vendor specific commands may be used here, as long as they are prefixed with a vendor key (as described in the ‘r’/’i’ commands) according to the following this syntax: &lt;vendorname&gt;:&lt;keyname&gt; The vendor-defined key may be any valid data type (int, float, string, char, binary). Example: Y iDirect: specialCmd=123</td><td></td><td>String</td></tr><tr><td>Additionally, a number of standard key-value pair commands are defined below.</td><td></td><td>(Options)</td></tr><tr><td>(Optional key-value format parameters)</td><td></td><td>extCmd=&lt;string cmd&gt;,</td></tr><tr><td>extCmd indicates to the antenna that it is to provide the modem with further information. The type of information requested is specified by parameter.</td><td></td><td>where cmd is one of {getConfigB,</td></tr><tr><td>Retrieve the extended ACU status string from the antenna. getExtTransceiverStatus. Get Extended Transceiver status</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>information from the antenna.</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>extCmdRepeatinterval indicates the repeat interval at which the antenna is to repeat the information. ‘0’ indicates that the information is only to be sent once. If this parameter is not specified, it is assumed to be ‘0’.</td><td></td><td>extCmdRepeatInterval=&lt;int seconds&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Modem Restart Reason (restartReason) Inform ACU of a pending reboot (SW updates, config file updates,</td><td></td><td>restartReason=&lt;string</td></tr><tr><td>and so on).</td><td></td><td>reason&gt;,</td></tr><tr><td>restartReason codes:</td><td></td><td>where ‘reason’ may be,</td></tr><tr><td>{noRestart,</td><td></td><td>{noRestart, modemSwUpdate,</td></tr><tr><td>modemSwUpdate,</td><td></td><td>modemConfigUpdate,</td></tr><tr><td>modemConfigUpdate,</td><td></td><td>mdoemReboot ,</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 30, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'parent_id': '9203fecb8253d23b88f1acb0e3e17b4d', 'category': 'Table', 'element_id': 'a4804d51f4716131fef3164d378bbdb9', 'is_table_fragment': False}, page_content='<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Miscellaneous and Custom Commands. ‘y’ command may to be used to send custom asynchronous messages to the antenna in a key- value pair formatted string. Vendor specific commands may be used here, as long as they are prefixed with a vendor key (as described in the ‘r’/’i’ commands) according to the following this syntax: &lt;vendorname&gt;:&lt;keyname&gt; The vendor-defined key may be any valid data type (int, float, string, char, binary). Example: Y iDirect: specialCmd=123</td><td></td><td>String</td></tr><tr><td>Additionally, a number of standard key-value pair commands are defined below.</td><td></td><td>(Options)</td></tr><tr><td>(Optional key-value format parameters)</td><td></td><td>extCmd=&lt;string cmd&gt;,</td></tr><tr><td>extCmd indicates to the antenna that it is to provide the modem with further information. The type of information requested is specified by parameter.</td><td></td><td>where cmd is one of {getConfigB,</td></tr><tr><td>Retrieve the extended ACU status string from the antenna. getExtTransceiverStatus. Get Extended Transceiver status</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>information from the antenna.</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>extCmdRepeatinterval indicates the repeat interval at which the antenna is to repeat the information. ‘0’ indicates that the information is only to be sent once. If this parameter is not specified, it is assumed to be ‘0’.</td><td></td><td>extCmdRepeatInterval=&lt;int seconds&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Modem Restart Reason (restartReason) Inform ACU of a pending reboot (SW updates, config file updates,</td><td></td><td>restartReason=&lt;string</td></tr><tr><td>and so on).</td><td></td><td>reason&gt;,</td></tr><tr><td>restartReason codes:</td><td></td><td>where ‘reason’ may be,</td></tr><tr><td>{noRestart,</td><td></td><td>{noRestart, modemSwUpdate,</td></tr><tr><td>modemSwUpdate,</td><td></td><td>modemConfigUpdate,</td></tr><tr><td>modemConfigUpdate,</td><td></td><td>mdoemReboot ,</td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5798083543777466, 'is_extracted': 'partial', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(368.58197021484375), np.float64(691.7747192382812)), (np.float64(368.58197021484375), np.float64(1037.0723876953125)), (np.float64(2604.03173828125), np.float64(1037.0723876953125)), (np.float64(2604.03173828125), np.float64(691.7747192382812))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T20:02:08', 'text_as_html': '<table><tbody><tr><td>a</td><td>alive interval</td><td></td><td>1</td><td>int repeat interval, seconds</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Antenna requests to see an L at least this often. 0 means "never</td><td>message from the modem repeat”.</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 32, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'parent_id': '105d5e615d8fc420c6b86e260140f91d', 'category': 'Table', 'element_id': '58f421a9da937205d4e68e6453513148', 'is_table_fragment': False}, page_content='<table><tbody><tr><td>a</td><td>alive interval</td><td></td><td>1</td><td>int repeat interval, seconds</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Antenna requests to see an L at least this often. 0 means "never</td><td>message from the modem repeat”.</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.49859634041786194, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(446.921875), np.float64(504.32098388671875)), (np.float64(446.921875), np.float64(2961.529541015625)), (np.float64(2699.6279296875), np.float64(2961.529541015625)), (np.float64(2699.6279296875), np.float64(504.32098388671875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T20:02:08', 'text_as_html': '<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>No. of Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="2">Status of the antenna. Antenna sends this immediately in response to the G command from the modem. The format of this response is meant to mirror that of the ‘s’ response, although not all parameters are</td><td>4</td><td>binary Antenna Functional:</td></tr><tr><td>(minimum)</td><td>1 - antenna functional</td></tr><tr><td>relevant. "Not functional" means that the antenna cannot currently operate and will never operate with this configuration. This can be temporary (for example, an illegal configuration) or permanent (for example, motor frozen).</td><td></td><td>0 - antenna not functional</td></tr><tr><td>“Modem must not transmit" means that the antenna has detected a condition (loss of lock, blockage, cable unwrap, max skew exceeded) that does not require a reconfiguration, but that does require the modem to cease transmission.</td><td></td><td>binary Modem May Transmit 1 - Modem may transmit 0 - Modem must not transmit int Search Count 0</td></tr><tr><td>The third parameter should be set to 0. (Search Count is not relevant when validating configuration commands).</td><td></td><td>(Always set to 0)</td></tr><tr><td>The fourth parameter ‘Tx Disabled’ should be set to 0. If an F command was sent more recently than an N command. If omitted, this parameter is assumed to be 0.</td><td></td><td>binary Tx Disabled: antenna (1 - has, 0 - has not) successfully disabled transmission toward the geosynchronous arc (response to N command). If this</td></tr><tr><td>NOTE: If the antenna cannot ensure it is ready for a transmitter test without regulatory violation, the fourth parameter should be set to 0.</td><td></td><td>parameter is "1" antenna is in a state to support installation tests such as power measurements; any power from the transmitter test is either terminated in a dummy load or otherwise prevented from</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>interfering with satellites.</td></tr><tr><td>The optional fifth parameter is an enumerated detailed status of the current antenna selected. (See Table 2-3, Enumerated Antenna Status Codes.)</td><td></td><td>int antenna_status 0 to 65535</td></tr><tr><td>The optional sixth parameter indicates to the modem the number of RF chains supported by the terminal. For single RF Chain (antenna) use cases, the value reported should be ‘1’. This parameter is an integer type with a range of [0 - n], where n is the number of RF chains antennas connected. (If this parameter is set to \'0\' the modem will infer that single antenna is connected)</td><td></td><td>int RF_chains int active RF chain index</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">The optional seventh parameter indicates to the modem the index of the active RF chain. For single antenna use cases, the value reported should be \'1\'. This parameter is an integer type with a range of [0 - n], where n is the number of antennas connected. (If this parameter is set to ‘0’ the modem will infer that single antenna is connected)</td></tr><tr><td>Time before Blockage (blockTime) This parameter should accompany status message 18, warning of an impending blockage. blockTime indicates the number of seconds remaining before the blockage is expected to occur. If the ‘G’ command was sent with an execution time specified, the blockTime will be reported relative to that execution time.</td><td></td><td>blockTime=&lt;int sec&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 33, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a0e3b69bd82fab4b676104a840c7460d', 'category': 'Table', 'element_id': 'a5d261ffcd2528b75b5892bf23701b0f', 'is_table_fragment': False}, page_content='<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>No. of Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="2">Status of the antenna. Antenna sends this immediately in response to the G command from the modem. The format of this response is meant to mirror that of the ‘s’ response, although not all parameters are</td><td>4</td><td>binary Antenna Functional:</td></tr><tr><td>(minimum)</td><td>1 - antenna functional</td></tr><tr><td>relevant. "Not functional" means that the antenna cannot currently operate and will never operate with this configuration. This can be temporary (for example, an illegal configuration) or permanent (for example, motor frozen).</td><td></td><td>0 - antenna not functional</td></tr><tr><td>“Modem must not transmit" means that the antenna has detected a condition (loss of lock, blockage, cable unwrap, max skew exceeded) that does not require a reconfiguration, but that does require the modem to cease transmission.</td><td></td><td>binary Modem May Transmit 1 - Modem may transmit 0 - Modem must not transmit int Search Count 0</td></tr><tr><td>The third parameter should be set to 0. (Search Count is not relevant when validating configuration commands).</td><td></td><td>(Always set to 0)</td></tr><tr><td>The fourth parameter ‘Tx Disabled’ should be set to 0. If an F command was sent more recently than an N command. If omitted, this parameter is assumed to be 0.</td><td></td><td>binary Tx Disabled: antenna (1 - has, 0 - has not) successfully disabled transmission toward the geosynchronous arc (response to N command). If this</td></tr><tr><td>NOTE: If the antenna cannot ensure it is ready for a transmitter test without regulatory violation, the fourth parameter should be set to 0.</td><td></td><td>parameter is "1" antenna is in a state to support installation tests such as power measurements; any power from the transmitter test is either terminated in a dummy load or otherwise prevented from</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>interfering with satellites.</td></tr><tr><td>The optional fifth parameter is an enumerated detailed status of the current antenna selected. (See Table 2-3, Enumerated Antenna Status Codes.)</td><td></td><td>int antenna_status 0 to 65535</td></tr><tr><td>The optional sixth parameter indicates to the modem the number of RF chains supported by the terminal. For single RF Chain (antenna) use cases, the value reported should be ‘1’. This parameter is an integer type with a range of [0 - n], where n is the number of RF chains antennas connected. (If this parameter is set to \'0\' the modem will infer that single antenna is connected)</td><td></td><td>int RF_chains int active RF chain index</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">The optional seventh parameter indicates to the modem the index of the active RF chain. For single antenna use cases, the value reported should be \'1\'. This parameter is an integer type with a range of [0 - n], where n is the number of antennas connected. (If this parameter is set to ‘0’ the modem will infer that single antenna is connected)</td></tr><tr><td>Time before Blockage (blockTime) This parameter should accompany status message 18, warning of an impending blockage. blockTime indicates the number of seconds remaining before the blockage is expected to occur. If the ‘G’ command was sent with an execution time specified, the blockTime will be reported relative to that execution time.</td><td></td><td>blockTime=&lt;int sec&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.41335242986679077, 'is_extracted': 'partial', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(452.87261962890625), np.float64(561.9216918945312)), (np.float64(452.87261962890625), np.float64(1949.8826904296875)), (np.float64(2626.734619140625), np.float64(1949.8826904296875)), (np.float64(2626.734619140625), np.float64(561.9216918945312))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T20:02:08', 'text_as_html': '<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(Optional key value pairs)</td><td></td><td>(Optional)</td></tr><tr><td>RF Terminal Type (rfTermType).</td><td></td><td>rfTermType=&lt;int&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">An integer identifying the RF Terminal Type assigned by</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">the network operator’s type approval process.</td></tr><tr><td>Range 1 to 32767.</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Antenna Serial Number (antennaSerial1No)</td><td></td><td>antennaSerialNo=&lt;string&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Antenna SW Rev (antennaSwRev)</td><td></td><td>antennaSwRev=&lt;string&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>In addition to the keys defined above, vendor specific</td><td></td><td>Vendor specific key</td></tr><tr><td>keys may be defined, following this syntax:</td><td></td><td>&lt;vendorname&gt;: keyname&gt;=&lt;int,</td></tr><tr><td>&lt;vendorname&gt;:&lt;keyname&gt;</td><td></td><td>float,string,char, or</td></tr><tr><td>The vendor-defined key may be any valid data type (int,</td><td></td><td>binary&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">float, string,char, binary).</td></tr><tr><td>Example:</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 35, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'parent_id': '20fda2b22cc7072c6d1ce754c97abf44', 'category': 'Table', 'element_id': 'd81e84692878582ac40ff25be2d6b816', 'is_table_fragment': False}, page_content='<table><thead><tr><th>Description</th><th>Parameter(s)</th><th>Name of the Parameters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(Optional key value pairs)</td><td></td><td>(Optional)</td></tr><tr><td>RF Terminal Type (rfTermType).</td><td></td><td>rfTermType=&lt;int&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">An integer identifying the RF Terminal Type assigned by</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">the network operator’s type approval process.</td></tr><tr><td>Range 1 to 32767.</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Antenna Serial Number (antennaSerial1No)</td><td></td><td>antennaSerialNo=&lt;string&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>Antenna SW Rev (antennaSwRev)</td><td></td><td>antennaSwRev=&lt;string&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>In addition to the keys defined above, vendor specific</td><td></td><td>Vendor specific key</td></tr><tr><td>keys may be defined, following this syntax:</td><td></td><td>&lt;vendorname&gt;: keyname&gt;=&lt;int,</td></tr><tr><td>&lt;vendorname&gt;:&lt;keyname&gt;</td><td></td><td>float,string,char, or</td></tr><tr><td>The vendor-defined key may be any valid data type (int,</td><td></td><td>binary&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">float, string,char, binary).</td></tr><tr><td>Example:</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5431011915206909, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(503.27716064453125), np.float64(598.1774291992188)), (np.float64(503.27716064453125), np.float64(2889.574462890625)), (np.float64(2684.26318359375), np.float64(2889.574462890625)), (np.float64(2684.26318359375), np.float64(598.1774291992188))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T20:02:08', 'text_as_html': '<table><tbody><tr><td>EIRP Spectral Density (ESD) calcuation information.</td><td>2 (minimum)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The reporting interval of this message from the Antenna is configured with the ‘reportingInterval’ parameter of the</td></tr><tr><td>‘R’ message. This message from the antenna includes the data</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>the modem needs for performing the calculation. The modem is</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>expected to enforce the ESD limit at the antenna/radome</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>output based on the ESDMax limit (esdMax), the symbol rate</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(Rs), modem output power, and RF chain gain information: esdMax = eirp - 10log(Rs / bandUnits)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The calculated EIRP is with</td></tr><tr><td>Spectral Density (ESD) compared ESD limit and modem transmission is set</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>power accordingly.</td><td>(optional)</td></tr><tr><td>value</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(Optional key pairs)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EIRP Spectral Density Maximum (esdMax)</td><td>esdMax=&lt;float dBW/bandUnits&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The current peak ESD of the antenna based on current skew</td></tr><tr><td>angle, scan angle and so on. ESD maximum is the peak EIRP</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>spectral density while in compliance with off-axis regulations</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" rowspan="2">such as FCC 25.218 and ETSI EN 303 978.</td></tr><tr><td>Units are dBW/bandUnits, where bandUnits is itself specified</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>below. If bandUnits is not specified, the bandwidth units are</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" rowspan="2">assumed to be 1Mhz. G/T (gt)</td></tr><tr><td>The current value of G/T in dB/K based on pointing angle. For</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>gt=&lt;float dB/K&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>mechanically steered antennas, this will usually be a constant. For Electronically steered arrays, it will vary with scan angle.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EIRP (eirp)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The current maximum value of EIRP in dBW based on pointing angle. For mechanically steered antennas, this will usually be a constant. For Electronically steered arrays, it will vary with scan angle. This may not be the EIRP that is currently being transmitted due to modem backoff and other factors</td><td>eirp=&lt;float dBW&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">Bandwidth Units (bandUnits)</td></tr><tr><td>Units of bandwidth for which the regulatory limit applies, that</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>is, 40kHz, 400kHz, 1000kHz (1Mhz). If not specified, it is</td><td>bandUnits=&lt;int kHz&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>assumed that units of bandwidth is 1000kHz(1MHz)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">Examples,</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">to select units of 400Khz, set bandUnits=400 to select units of 1Mhz, set bandUnits=1000</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>skewAngle=&lt;float degrees&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 36, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'parent_id': '5c32c3c48ada35a8960a912d7a6dbddb', 'category': 'Table', 'element_id': 'a6c71a7c24d6aadedbe5d700465a7b11', 'is_table_fragment': False}, page_content='<table><tbody><tr><td>EIRP Spectral Density (ESD) calcuation information.</td><td>2 (minimum)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The reporting interval of this message from the Antenna is configured with the ‘reportingInterval’ parameter of the</td></tr><tr><td>‘R’ message. This message from the antenna includes the data</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>the modem needs for performing the calculation. The modem is</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>expected to enforce the ESD limit at the antenna/radome</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>output based on the ESDMax limit (esdMax), the symbol rate</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(Rs), modem output power, and RF chain gain information: esdMax = eirp - 10log(Rs / bandUnits)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The calculated EIRP is with</td></tr><tr><td>Spectral Density (ESD) compared ESD limit and modem transmission is set</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>power accordingly.</td><td>(optional)</td></tr><tr><td>value</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(Optional key pairs)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EIRP Spectral Density Maximum (esdMax)</td><td>esdMax=&lt;float dBW/bandUnits&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">The current peak ESD of the antenna based on current skew</td></tr><tr><td>angle, scan angle and so on. ESD maximum is the peak EIRP</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>spectral density while in compliance with off-axis regulations</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" rowspan="2">such as FCC 25.218 and ETSI EN 303 978.</td></tr><tr><td>Units are dBW/bandUnits, where bandUnits is itself specified</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>below. If bandUnits is not specified, the bandwidth units are</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" rowspan="2">assumed to be 1Mhz. G/T (gt)</td></tr><tr><td>The current value of G/T in dB/K based on pointing angle. For</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>gt=&lt;float dB/K&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>mechanically steered antennas, this will usually be a constant. For Electronically steered arrays, it will vary with scan angle.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>EIRP (eirp)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The current maximum value of EIRP in dBW based on pointing angle. For mechanically steered antennas, this will usually be a constant. For Electronically steered arrays, it will vary with scan angle. This may not be the EIRP that is currently being transmitted due to modem backoff and other factors</td><td>eirp=&lt;float dBW&gt;</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">Bandwidth Units (bandUnits)</td></tr><tr><td>Units of bandwidth for which the regulatory limit applies, that</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>is, 40kHz, 400kHz, 1000kHz (1Mhz). If not specified, it is</td><td>bandUnits=&lt;int kHz&gt;</td></tr><tr><td>assumed that units of bandwidth is 1000kHz(1MHz)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">Examples,</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">to select units of 400Khz, set bandUnits=400 to select units of 1Mhz, set bandUnits=1000</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>skewAngle=&lt;float degrees&gt;</td></tr></tbody></table>'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_d9819300d88ddfd3ced0bb7e3d1398ac.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8686432838439941, 'is_extracted': 'partial', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(357.6224060058594), np.float64(535.2301025390625)), (np.float64(357.6224060058594), np.float64(1530.480224609375)), (np.float64(2608.49658203125), np.float64(1530.480224609375)), (np.float64(2608.49658203125), np.float64(535.2301025390625))), 'system': 'Pixe